This demonstration is one of the first application where we consider a large network
of GNSS receivers using our powerful GNSS-Qc processor.

In this example we deploy several NTRIP clients
(input side), because GNSS-Qc is a true MISO (Multi Input Single Output) processor, it is able to
absorb, synchronize and process all these data sources. In this example, we focus on dual frequency
code range and phase observations on each individual sites. We deploy the QcTecProcessor which
consumes the raw observations and evaluate the Vertical Total Electron Content (VTEC) on each site location.

The network we will use is centipede.fr which offers a large amount of reference sites, originally dedicated to RTK
([Real Time Kinematics](../documentation/RTK.md)). Each data source is labelled according to its position and the official
reference site (often times referred to as "Marker" name).

The network covers Western Europe and mostly France, we will compute the regional VTEC over the course of 2 hours (two complete hours of measurements gathering
and computations).
